cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, cite it as below."
title: "NeuroBranch: leakage-safe C. elegans dynamics and bounded virtual-perturbation evaluation"
abstract: >-
  NeuroBranch is a research platform for C. elegans whole-brain population
  dynamics, latent branching and model-dependent virtual perturbation. Version
  1.2.0 adds a hierarchical measurement audit, animal-cluster benchmark inference
  and a model-conditional design table. The hierarchical posterior failed its
  calibration gates, so the coverage-aware 0.560 ceiling remains descriptive and
  no calibrated interval or ranking is claimed. Intervention outputs are
  model-dependent and are not causally validated.
authors:
  - name: "NeuroBranch contributors"
version: "1.2.0"
date-released: "2026-10-30"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - computational neuroscience
  - C. elegans
  - calcium imaging
  - optogenetics
  - reliability
  - benchmark
type: software
